From 2e5fc1e54ae55f293eb045d85446690699f10615 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Williams <gregory.williams@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 20 Aug 2025 16:53:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 054/190] misc: xilinx-ai-engine: Clear disable tlast bit

commit ba0190e5314348974b8df0f1bfa0b50df7f71288 from
https://github.com/Xilinx/linux-xlnx.git xlnx_rebase_v6.12

When calling disable tlast pm op, it is not getting cleared correctly
causing a warning at the end of the call.

Signed-off-by: Gregory Williams <gregory.williams@amd.com>
Acked-by: Govindarajulu Varadarajan <govindarajulu.varadarajan@amd.com>
Message-ID: <20250820235329.500334-2-gregory.williams@amd.com>
State: pending
Signed-off-by: Quanyang Wang <quanyang.wang@windriver.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-pm.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-pm.c b/drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-pm.c
index 78d2902c8b47..cfa419899641 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-pm.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/xilinx-ai-engine/ai-engine-pm.c
@@ -414,7 +414,7 @@ int aie_part_pm_ops(struct aie_partition *apart, void *data, u32 type, struct ai
 				return ret;
 			goto again;
 		}
-		type &= AIE_PART_INIT_OPT_DIS_TLAST_ERROR;
+		type &= ~AIE_PART_INIT_OPT_DIS_TLAST_ERROR;
 		op = pm_ops->pkt_va + pm_ops->offset;
 		pm_ops->offset += sizeof(*op);
 		op->type = XILINX_AIE_OPS_CTRL_PKT_TLAST_ERR;
-- 
2.43.0

